# Database

The shape of the schema, in one place. Domain language is in
[CONTEXT.md](../CONTEXT.md), the models standing on these tables are in
[app/models/CLAUDE.md](../app/models/CLAUDE.md), and the decisions behind both
are in [docs/adr/](../docs/adr/). This file is the picture: what tables exist,
how they join, and which rules the database itself enforces.

**Schema version: `<!-- TODO: version -->`** — the `define(version:)` line at
the top of [schema.rb](schema.rb). If it doesn't match, this document is stale;
see [CLAUDE.md](CLAUDE.md) for the rule that keeps it honest.

The schema is drawn in clusters rather than one sheet, because one sheet with
every table on it is unreadable. Hub tables may appear in more than one
diagram; there is still only one of each.

| Cluster | Tables |
| --- | --- |
| [Identity](#identity) | `users`, `sessions` |
<% if stripe? -%>
| [Payments](#payments) | `stripe_events` |
<% end -%>
<!-- TODO: One row per cluster, linking to its section below. -->

## Identity

Generated by the Rails authentication generator<%= ", extended for 2FA" if two_factor? %>.

```mermaid
erDiagram
    users ||--o{ sessions : ""
```

| Table | Columns | Rules in the database |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `users` | `email_address`, `password_digest`<%= ", `otp_secret`" if two_factor? %> | `email_address` and `password_digest` not null; unique `email_address` |
| `sessions` | `user_id`, `ip_address`, `user_agent` | `user_id` not null, foreign key to `users` |
<% if two_factor? -%>

`otp_secret` is null until the user enables 2FA, and that absence is what
`two_factor_enabled?` reads. It is encrypted **in Ruby** (Active Record
encryption), so the database only ever holds ciphertext.
<% end -%>
<% if stripe? -%>

## Payments

Webhook events from Stripe, stored once and processed by a job.

```mermaid
erDiagram
    stripe_events
```

| Table | Columns | Rules in the database |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `stripe_events` | `stripe_id`, `event_type`, `payload` (jsonb), `processed_at` | `stripe_id`, `event_type` and `payload` not null; unique `stripe_id`; indexed `processed_at` |

The unique `stripe_id` is what makes a redelivered webhook a no-op.
`processed_at` stays null until the event is handled, including when handling
fails; processed events are deleted after 90 days.
<% end -%>

<!-- TODO: One section per cluster, in the format above. -->

## Framework tables

Not diagrammed, not ours to shape:

<% if llm? -%>
- `chats`, `messages` and the `ruby_llm_*` tables — created by RubyLLM
  (`ruby_llm:install` and the gem's own migrations). `chats` and `messages`
  move into a cluster above once the app builds its own behaviour on them.
- `active_storage_blobs` / `_attachments` / `_variant_records` — uploads,
  installed with RubyLLM. Must stay in **proxy mode** so blobs are served from
  our own origin (see the CSP rules in the root CLAUDE.md).
<% else -%>
- Active Storage is not installed. If it is added, it must stay in **proxy
  mode** so blobs are served from our own origin (see the CSP rules in the
  root CLAUDE.md).
<% end -%>
- Solid Queue, Cache and Cable each own a separate PostgreSQL database with its
  own schema file: [queue_schema.rb](queue_schema.rb),
  [cache_schema.rb](cache_schema.rb), [cable_schema.rb](cable_schema.rb).

## Deletion

No foreign key carries an `ON DELETE` clause unless listed here. Deletion is
guarded in the models instead — the rules, and the few deliberate exceptions,
are in [app/models/CLAUDE.md](../app/models/CLAUDE.md).

